IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa30-regulative`

-- coa30-tests-regulative.l4: traces of the regulative rules of coa30-regulative.l4. A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with
-- EQUALS in an #ASSERT on the stable binary, and a #TRACE prints no assertion line, so check.sh counts none for this file.
-- The result expected from the text is written above each trace, and the result the binary printed is recorded in NOTES.md
-- (section "Regulative rules: traces"). The decision-function twin of each rule is asserted in the module named in the
-- regulative module's comment, and that is where the counted assertions are.
-- The #EVAL lines evaluate a constant (the rule is a constant, a DEONTIC value) so that the result is printed.

§ `Traces: Schedules 10 to 13`

-- sch 10 para 2(4): the Secretary of State refuses and gives the notice: FULFILLED. Gives none: the LEST fires (BREACH).
#TRACE `sch 10 para 2(4) the notice of refusal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 2(4) give the applicant a written notice of the refusal` AT 1
#EVAL `sch 10 para 2(4) the notice of refusal`

-- sch 10 para 3(3): all three before revoking: FULFILLED. The notice is given and published but no steps are taken for the members: still owed.
#TRACE `sch 10 para 3(3) the duties before revoking` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(3)(a) give written notice of the intention to revoke to the recognised body` AT 1
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(3)(b) take reasonably practicable steps to bring the notice to the attention of the members` AT 2
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(3)(c) publish the notice` AT 3

#TRACE `sch 10 para 3(3) the duties before revoking` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(3)(a) give written notice of the intention to revoke to the recognised body` AT 1
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(3)(c) publish the notice` AT 3

-- sch 10 para 3(5): a person within (6) acts in month 2 (inside the three months): FULFILLED. In month 4 (outside them): the permission has lapsed and the event is passed over.
#TRACE `sch 10 para 3(5) the permission to make representations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) a person within paragraph 3(6)` DOES `sch 10 para 3(5) make written or oral representations` AT 2

#TRACE `sch 10 para 3(5) the permission to make representations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) a person within paragraph 3(6)` DOES `sch 10 para 3(5) make written or oral representations` AT 4

-- sch 10 para 3(11): all three on making the order: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `sch 10 para 3(11) the duties on making the order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(11)(a) give written notice of the making of the order to the body` AT 0
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(11)(b) take reasonably practicable steps to bring the making of the order to the attention of the members` AT 1
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 10 para 3(11)(c) publish a notice of the making of the order` AT 2

-- sch 10 para 13(12): a summary delivered in month 9 of the year: FULFILLED. Nothing by month 13: BREACH.
#TRACE `sch 10 para 13(12) the annual summary` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the recognised supervisory body` DOES `sch 10 para 13(12) deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections` AT 9

#TRACE `sch 10 para 13(12) the annual summary` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 13)

-- sch 10 para 20ZA, sch 12 para 4: the duty to pay: paid, FULFILLED.
#TRACE `sch 10 para 20ZA the duty to pay the costs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the recognised supervisory body` DOES `sch 10 para 20ZA pay the costs incurred by the competent authority or another recognised supervisory body` AT 5

#TRACE `sch 12 para 4 the duty to pay the costs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the registered third country auditor` DOES `sch 12 para 4 pay the costs of maintaining the relevant arrangements` AT 5

-- sch 13 para 8(1): "immediately": at the instant the instrument is made, FULFILLED; one tick later, BREACH.
#TRACE `sch 13 para 8(1) the duty to make the instrument available` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the body designated by the delegation order` DOES `sch 13 para 8(1) print the instrument and make it available to the public` AT 0

#TRACE `sch 13 para 8(1) the duty to make the instrument available` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1)

-- sch 13 para 9(3), 10(1), 10(3)
#TRACE `sch 13 para 9(3) the duty to endorse a copy` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the body designated by the delegation order` DOES `sch 13 para 9(3) cause a copy of the instrument to be endorsed with a certificate` AT 3

#TRACE `sch 13 para 10(1) the annual report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the body designated by the delegation order` DOES `sch 13 para 10(1) make a report to the Secretary of State` AT 11

#TRACE `sch 13 para 10(1) the annual report` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 13)

#TRACE `sch 13 para 10(3) the duty to lay the report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State` DOES `sch 13 para 10(3) lay copies of the report before Parliament` AT 6
